hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"18049","Yaqub narrated to us, my father narrated to us from Ibn Ishaq, he said: Imran ibn Abi Anas narrated to me from Hanzalah ibn Ali al-Aslami from a man from Banu al-Dil, he said: I prayed noon in my house, then I went out with camels of mine to send them forth to the herdsman, then I passed by the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was praying noon with the people, so I went on and did not pray with him, then when I had sent forth my camels and returned, that was mentioned to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), then he said to me: What prevented you, O so-and-so, from praying with us when you passed by us. He said: Then I said: O Messenger of Allah, I had prayed in my house. He said: And even if."
